{"author":{"id":"f4f7e123ea38957901744390924e1710825e6d55b5113472173231f66fb2d926"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777790203,"nonce":"BTsL0jADoxDgm3+KWkFeU4hHo8k=","title":"Outreach: Show HN / Lobsters writeup of GW-BASIC 2026","message":"Highest-leverage discovery move. GW-BASIC nostalgia is enormous (every Gen-X/late-Boomer programmer started on BASIC); paired with the 'Microsoft 2020 source release → modern C11 reimplementation' angle, this is a near-guaranteed HN front-page candidate.\n\nAngle: 'Reimplementing GW-BASIC in modern C from the 1983 assembly Microsoft released in 2020.' The combination (authoritative reference + clean reimplementation, not transpilation + bug-compatible behavior + AOT compiler) is the technical hook; the BASIC nostalgia is the emotional hook.\n\nRequired content:\n- Brief history: GW-BASIC's role in the IBM PC era (1983-1988+), why Microsoft released the 8088 assembly in 2020, what 'reimplementation not transpilation' means and why it matters\n- Architecture: clean C11, modern data structures, three build targets (interpreter, AOT compiler, runtime library)\n- Bug-compatibility as engineering choice: what quirks of the original were preserved deliberately, why\n- Demo: side-by-side run of a vintage BASIC program (something culturally familiar — Hammurabi, Lemonade Stand, Snake) on original GW-BASIC under DOSBox vs. GW-BASIC 2026; show identical output\n- AOT compiler path: BASIC source → native binary, not just interpreted — a non-obvious feature that distinguishes from many other BASIC revivals\n- Optional sound (SOUND/BEEP/PLAY) via PulseAudio — small but charming\n- License: MIT (much friendlier story than GPL for HN audience)\n- Roadmap teaser: FreeDOS package (issue 081c01c), DOS/Windows port\n\nSubmission venues:\n1. Lobste.rs (retrocomputing, c, basic tags)\n2. HN Show HN — strong front-page candidate given subject\n3. r/programming, r/retrobattlestations, r/QBasic\n4. atariage / vogons software-development forums\n5. Microsoft GW-BASIC repo (issue or discussion linking back) — not spammy if framed as 'related project'\n\nCoordination: this should land before or with the FreeDOS package release (issue 081c01c) and the FreeDOS community submission (issue ab8188c) so all the inbound traffic from each lands on a project with a polished public face.","files":null}]}